course: dictionary
lesson: 5330
title: One word, two worlds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Keyboard is a good example. It can mean the keys you press to type on a computer, tablet or phone, or the row of black and white keys on a piano.
explain: Look for clues. If the sentence is about typing, letters or the screen, keyboard means the keys you type on. If it is about notes, tunes or playing a song, keyboard means the piano-style keys.
explain: Test your meaning in the sentence. «Press a key on the laptop and a letter pops up on the screen» only makes sense with the typing meaning. «She played a tune on the keyboard» only makes sense with the music meaning.
explain: Phrases are clues too. A keyboard shortcut is a quick key press that does a job, and an on-screen keyboard is a keyboard shown on a screen that you tap or click.
fact: A keyboard is a set of keys you press to type into a computer, tablet or phone.
fact: A keyboard is also the row of black and white keys on a piano.
fact: Most English keyboards use the QWERTY layout, named after the first six letters in the top row.
fact: «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» is a pangram, because it uses every letter of the alphabet.
fact: An electronic keyboard is a musical instrument with piano keys, and in a band it often plays chords.
exercise: «Press a key on the laptop and a letter pops up on the screen.» What is the keyboard in this sentence? | The list of shortcuts on the screen | *The set of keys you press to type | The member of the band who sings | The row of black and white keys on a piano
exercise: «She played a tune on the keyboard in the music lesson.» What does keyboard mean here? | A computer screen | A type of drum | A list of shortcuts | *An instrument with piano keys
exercise: Which phrase means a quick key press that does a job? | Band keyboard | *Keyboard shortcut | Pangram | Keyboard instrument
test: What does a pangram use? | Only the vowels | Only the numbers from 1 to 9 | *Every letter of the alphabet | Every word from a dictionary
test: Why is «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» used to test keyboards? | Because it is the longest sentence in the world | *Because it uses every letter of the alphabet | Because it is a song about a fox | Because it has no vowels
exam: Which meaning of keyboard fits this sentence: «The keyboard sends a signal in, the computer works out which letter it is, and the screen shows it»? | An instrument that plays a tune | The black and white keys on a piano | A pangram | *The keys you press to type
